{
  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "The current best (config_049: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, 0.725 acc) sits in the clearly dominant family (scvi_n200 >> scgpt, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, multiprofile >> singleprofile). The only untested combination within this top family is transformer aggregation with concat fusion (config_011). While weighted fusion has outperformed concat in other settings (config_007 vs 016: 0.542 vs 0.518), transformer aggregation already performs an attention-weighted combination of profile tokens, so concat may provide complementary raw information that a subsequent linear layer can exploit differently. Testing config_011 completes the 2×2 aggregation×fusion grid for the best encoder pair, directly clarifying whether 0.725 is the ceiling for this family or whether a small fusion-method gain is available. With 3 experiments left, locking in the optimal fusion for the top family is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve. Expected cost: moderate (~4–5 GPU hours), comparable to config_049 (3.60) but slightly higher due to the larger concatenated feature vector, consistent with the concat premium seen in config_016 (7.18) vs config_007 (2.94)."
}

